@api @smoke\nFeature: User API Testing\n\n  @get-user\n  Scenario: Get single user successfully\n    Given the API base URL is \"https://reqres.in/api\"\n    When the user sends GET request to \"/users/1\"\n    Then the response status code should be 200\n    And the response should contain user with id 1\n\n  @get-users\n  Scenario: Get list of users with pagination\n    Given the API base URL is \"https://reqres.in/api\"\n    When the user sends GET request to \"/users?page=1\"\n    Then the response status code should be 200\n    And the response should contain a list of users\n    And the response should have pagination data\n\n  @create-user\n  Scenario: Create user successfully\n    Given the API base URL is \"https://reqres.in/api\"\n    When the user sends POST request to \"/users\" with body:\n      | name | email |\n      | John | john@example.com |\n    Then the response status code should be 201\n    And the response should contain user id\n\n  @update-user\n  Scenario: Update user successfully\n    Given the API base URL is \"https://reqres.in/api\"\n    When the user sends PUT request to \"/users/2\" with updated data\n    Then the response status code should be 200\n    And the response should contain updated user\n\n  @delete-user @negative\n  Scenario: Delete user successfully\n    Given the API base URL is \"https://reqres.in/api\"\n    When the user sends DELETE request to \"/users/2\"\n    Then the response status code should be 204\n\n  @invalid-user @negative\n  Scenario: Get non-existent user\n    Given the API base URL is \"https://reqres.in/api\"\n    When the user sends GET request to \"/users/999\"\n    Then the response status code should be 404\n\n  @invalid-payload @negative\n  Scenario: Create user with invalid payload\n    Given the API base URL is \"https://reqres.in/api\"\n    When the user sends POST request to \"/users\" with invalid body\n    Then the response status code should be 400\n"